Last week there was a thread about converting altars but without a
real decisive conclusion, so I thought I'd relate my recent experience.

I was playing a Barbarian (chaotic) and I killed an orange dragon.
Since I already had some orange dragon scale mail, I left it in
the hall (after eating as much of it as I could).  Anyway, a short distance
away I found a lawful temple.  So, I dropped enough junk to allow me
to pick up the halfeaten dragon, and brought it in to sacrifice.

Ok.  I'm a newbie, but I read these posts which keep talking about people
who have both Stormbringer and Excalibur, which seems impossible to me,
so I thought maybe this was how they did it.

Anyway, I sacrificed the dragon and got the 'you sense a conflict between
whoever and morrigan' and I thought, oops, but then it said 'you feel
morrigan has increased in power'  then 'the altar before you turn black'
or something like that.  And it was a morrigan (chaotic) altar.

Could it be that as long as you sacrifice a big enough monster, you can
convert any alter to your religion?

Just my 2 cents.

